<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Command staff</div>
      <h2>The people behind the models</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="person">
      <div class="person-photo">
        <img src="/images/Manoj0.jpeg" alt="Manoj Tadepalli"
          style="transform: scale(1.9) translateY(-15%); transform-origin: top center;" /><span
          class="id-tag">Co-Founder
          &amp;
          CEO</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Manoj Tadepalli</h3>
        <span class="role">Co-Founder &amp; Chief Executive Officer</span>
        <p>
          A co-founder, Manoj is the marketing and retail domain lead of
          RainMan. He has led the effort to make RainMan’s services more oriented
          to marketing, taking it into promotions and pricing analytics as well
          as deep dives for distribution. He has also conceptualised the
          marketing datamart and scenario planner which allows companies to move
          quickly into a high level of marketing analytics deployment, while
          scaling up to a company-wide deployment. He has also worked to make
          marketing analytics more relevant for retailers by bringing in new
          variables such as festival impact and environmental factors leading to
          predictive models. He has been the lead on a number of RainMan’s
          accounts including Johnson & Johnson, Titan and Wipro among others.
        </p>
        <details class="bio">
          <p>
            Starting as an Account Manager and Planner at Ogilvy and FCB ULKA,
            Manoj's 25 years of experience has given him a deep grounding in
            branding, product management, distribution and innovation
            management. As head of marketing at Titan Industries, Manoj
            spearheaded the successful turnaround of the Titan brand and the
            relaunch of Fastrack and Xylys, Titan's premium brands. As a
            business head in international markets, he planned and executed
            Titan's forays into Southeast Asia and the United States, where his
            team that launched Tanishq won the Tata Group's prestigious Innovity
            award. Manoj was also Country Manager at Enterprise IG for India and
            built corporate and brand identities for key Indian companies during
            his tenure there.
          </p>
          <summary></summary>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="person">
      <div class="person-photo balu-photo">
        <img src="/images/Balu0.jpeg" alt="V Balasubramanium" style="object-position: center 20%;" /><span
          class="id-tag">Co-Founder &amp; MD</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>V Balasubramanium ( Balu )</h3>
        <span class="role">Co-Founder &amp; Managing Director</span>
        <p>
          Co-founder of RainMan Consulting, Balu also functions as the media
          domain lead of RainMan. He engages with key clients and has been
          associated with multiple media investment management project
          implementations. Balu also conceptualised RainMan's analytic benchmark
          tool, RainGauge. Balu has spent more than 15 years of his career with
          WPP agencies like JWT, Ogilvy and GroupM in India, China and Global in
          the media planning, consumer insights and analytics functions. His
          major responsibility was to create a discipline for marketing
          performance management with analytics at the heart of the process. As
          Global Chief Executive Officer of Meritus Analytics Pvt. Ltd. (now
          Gain Theory) a WPP analytic insights consultancy, Balu was responsible
          for the set up and the growth of Meritus, making it a top global
          knowledge focused and consulting company. Prior to joining Meritus,
          Balu was Director, Advanced Techniques Group (ATG) and Insights for
          GroupM South Asia.
        </p>
        <details class="bio">
          <p>
            He was a core executive committee member who set up and steered
            GroupM in South Asia. He conceived and set up the Global Analytic
            Centre (GAC), providing advanced analytics for GroupM Worldwide
            clients. Balu also had a stint with GroupM China in the late 90's to
            set up its marketing analytics practice. Prior to joining GroupM
            South Asia, Balu was Managing Consultant, Strategy Planning and
            Media Development at Ogilvy India for six years. He implemented
            global standard media tools, planning processes and insight
            solutions for key clients of Ogilvy India, besides creating a
            consulting business within the agency. Balu also functioned as a
            media planning professional with JWT, Bangalore and Mudra
            Communications, Ahmedabad. Balu is the winner of the prestigious WPP
            Global Atticus Grand Prix in 1999 for authoring a strategy paper
            called "Measuring Passion". Atticus Grand Prix is a global
            prestigious award for excellence in original published thinking in
            marketing service discipline instituted by WPP Inc.
          </p>
          <summary></summary>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="person">
      <div class="person-photo">
        <img src="/images/KK0.jpeg" alt="Krishna Kumar CS"
          style="transform: scale(1.25) translateY(-3%); transform-origin: top center;" /><span class="id-tag">Chief
          Analytics Officer</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Krishna Kumar CS ( KK )</h3>
        <span class="role">Chief Analytics Officer &amp; Director</span>

        <p>
          KK heads the analytics practice in RainMan. KK's key responsibility in
          RainMan is to bring innovation in analytic techniques and to deploy
          the best and latest of the techniques for actionable insights. KK has
          been responsible in successfully implementing a variety of new
          approaches to solve many marketing problems. Empowered with in depth
          knowledge in direct marketing analytics, KK has been implementing a
          variety of successful projects in the area of digital marketing and e
          commerce. KK's first brush with data-heavy projects began in the
          infancy of analytics, at Ogilvy Direct in the early 1990's.
        </p>
        <details class="bio">
          <p>
            He has since been a pioneer in the field. After setting up Ogilvy's
            first analytics team and working with some of its key global
            clients, he successfully took his expertise to Covansys (now CSC)
            and Reliance ADAG. KK blends an in-depth knowledge of statistics, IT
            and marketing with an evangelical belief of using technology and
            statistics to derive insights from data. A master of Marketing Mix
            Modelling (MMM), he has worked on global and local brands. KK has a
            unique way of looking at modelling processes and has introduced many
            new methodologies in this area. He is also a visiting faculty in
            Analytics at the Narsee Monjee Institute of Management Studies
            (Bangalore Campus).
          </p>
          <summary></summary>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="person">
      <div class="person-photo">
        <img src="/images/Gideon0.jpeg" alt="Gideon Anthony D'Souza"
          style="transform: scale(1.85) translateY(-14%); transform-origin: top center;" /><span class="id-tag">Manager
          Data and
          Technology</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Gideon Anthony D'Souza</h3>
        <span class="role">Manager Data and Technology</span>

        <p>
          As the Manager – Data & Technology at RainMan, he leads the development of
          analytics platforms, AI-driven solutions, and decision intelligence
          applications. He works on building scalable technology solutions that
          support marketing analytics and help clients make informed business
          decisions. He contributes across software development, data
          engineering, and analytics, working closely with business and
          technical teams to develop and enhance the company's technology
          platforms. His interests include artificial intelligence, data-driven
          systems, and the applications of engineering principles to solve
          business problems.
        </p>
        <details class="bio">
          <p>
            Prior to joining RainMan, he worked on engineering research and
            analytics projects in ocean engineering and signal analytics at the
            Indian Institute of Technology Madras. He subsequently worked at
            Britannia Industries in data analytics, gaining experience in
            business intelligence for the FMCG sector. His multidisciplinary
            background enables him to combine engineering principles with
            advanced analytics to solve complex business challenges. He holds a
            Master of Science in Mechatronics Engineering from De Montfort
            University, Leicester, United Kingdom, and a Bachelor of Engineering
            in Electronics & Communication Engineering. With over nine years of
            experience spanning data analytics, software engineering, artificial
            intelligence, and decision intelligence, he brings a
            multidisciplinary approach to developing technology solutions for
            business challenges.
          </p>
          <summary></summary>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="person">
      <div class="person-photo">
        <img src="/images/Yesh0.jpeg" alt="Yeshwanth Raj"
          style="transform: scale(1.35); transform-origin: top center;" /><span class="id-tag">Manager Analytics</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Yeshwanth Raj</h3>
        <span class="role">Manager Analytics</span>
        <p>
          As Analytics Manager at RainMan Consulting, Yeshwanth Raj leads our
          Market Mix Modelling work for CPG and FMCG clients turning "what
          happened" into "what to do next." He translates regression, Bayesian,
          and machine learning-based models into budget and channel decisions
          that hold up under real business constraints, not just clean slides.
          He brings 6+ years in MMM across RainMan and Nielsen, working the full
          model lifecycle: design and validation, decomposing short- vs.
          long-term marketing effects (including Kalman filter-based
          estimation), brand equity modelling, and media network analysis. He is just as comfortable defending a model
          to a client's CFO as he is building it.
        </p>
        <details class="bio">
          <p>
            He started at RainMan as an Analyst, spent two years at Nielsen
            managing MMM projects and delivery teams for global CPG clients,
            then came back to RainMan first as Senior Analyst, now as
            Analytics Manager. That mix of specialist-firm depth and
            global-measurement-leader scale is exactly why clients trust his
            team's numbers. As Analytics Manager, Yeshwanth owns delivery
            end-to-end leading and mentoring the team, running client
            relationships, and keeping projects on scope, on time, on budget.
            He's known for keeping a level head under pressure and giving his
            team the calm, steady direction that gets projects across the line,
            even when timelines get tight. He holds a Master of Science in
            Statistics from Loyola College. He builds models that change
            decisions — not just decks.
          </p>
          <summary></summary>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="person">
      <div class="person-photo">
        <img src="/images/Aman0.jpeg" alt="Amandeep Singh"
          style="transform: scale(1.65) translateY(-7%); transform-origin: top center;" /><span class="id-tag">Manager
          Analytics</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Amandeep Singh</h3>
        <span class="role">Manager Analytics</span>
        <p>
          As Manager of Analytics, Amandeep brings together three disciplines in
          one: the precision of an engineer, the rigor of a statistician, and
          the instinct of a marketer. Backed by a BE in Computer Science with a specialization in AI/ML and nearly three
          years in marketing analytics, he
          doesn't just report on performance — he builds the systems that improve
          it. He writes the code, designs and deploys automated algorithms that
          cut manual effort, and applies statistical depth to separate signal
          from noise, so every decision rests on evidence rather than guesswork.
          Whether it's uncovering what truly drives a campaign or forecasting
          where to invest next, he stays focused on the outcomes that move the
          business forward.
        </p>
        <details class="bio">
          <p>
            His proudest work is RainBrain, an intelligent analytics solution he
            designed, built on his own from concept to code. It reflects how he
            likes to work: taking an idea end to end and turning it into
            something that delivers real impact. His principle is simple: jack
            of all trades, master of impact.
          </p>
          <summary></summary>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

